Presence of this file opts the project into the protoblast plugin's checkPrivateSettingsContexts
compile gate (production Java constructing a SettingsContext of its own: the default settings
chain loads into Zenit.SETTINGS_VALUES and nothing else, so a module's private context accepts
every configured value and never reads one; see CheckPrivateSettingsContextsTask). A settings
tree with files of its own carries a "private-settings-context: <why>" comment.
